    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.85), who provide the highest efficiency scores of the day. **Soderstrom** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against a favorable 5.31 xERA matchup, while **Moniak** is a high-upside play driven by a 14% platoon edge and significant park factor enhancements. Similarly, **James Wood** (69.19) remains a priority start; his elite 0.425 xwOBA combined with a prime leadoff spot and a 14% park factor boost makes him an essential anchor for our run production. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.63) also secures a strong position in the UTIL slot, fueled by a 14% dynamic platoon advantage against Roupp.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Naylor** (59.33), who fell just shy of displacing our lower-scoring starters. While **Naylor** projects well, his 5% park penalty and a negative BvP historical trend (28 PA) pushed the optimizer to favor the higher efficiency floors provided by the likes of **Jose Caballero** (60.94) and **Isaac Paredes** (61.80). Conversely, **Corbin Carroll** (58.95) remains in the lineup despite a sub-60 score; in our league, his elite speed profile forces us to prioritize his stolen base potential over pure raw projection, as the scarcity of the category dictates his inclusion regardless of the tough matchup against Jump.\n\nOperational risks persist, most notably for **Austin Riley** (64.88), where a 35% rain risk adds a layer of volatility to an otherwise strong matchup. We are also monitoring the lineup status for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**; while both are penciled in, their efficiency relies heavily on their confirmed order position. We continue to hold **Zach McKinstry** and **Edwin Arroyo** on the bench, as their sub-50 projections and specific wind/order penalties make them unsuitable for this rotation. We will watch **Austin Riley** closely as the weather report develops, but for now, the roster remains set to maximize our 5x5 categories.",
